# PR146: internal research deliverables of the public-demo campaign (PR139-PR145).
# Criterion: every path below is untracked, quoted by no tracked file, and is either an internal
# report, a measured payload of the regression documents, a build copy of the HF package, a Gradio
# temp-file cache, or a nested Git object store (rollback-bare/, gh-clone/, hf-deploy/).
# 531 files and ~71 MB on disk, of which 393 were still stageable by `git add .` when PR145 measured
# them. None of it is destined for the repository. Each pattern contains a slash, so it is anchored
# to this directory; results/product-review137/ is deliberately not covered (two tracked files).
results/product-review139/
results/product-review140/
results/product-review141/
results/product-review142/
results/product-review143/
results/product-review144/
results/product-review145/

# PR147: re-inclusion de l'outillage de validation independante (PR110) et de sa fermeture de
# dependances, pour qu'un nouveau poste puisse reconstruire la porte `python scripts/pr110_ready.py`.
# La mesure AST de results/product-review147/pr147_closure.py montre que les six scripts PR110
# importent transitivement dix harnais de recherche PR103-PR109 : suivre les six sans les dix ne
# deplace l'erreur que d'un cran (lecon PR118, FileNotFoundError -> ModuleNotFoundError).
# Ces regles de fichiers individuelles viennent du bloc PR135 ; la priorite « la derniere regle qui
# correspond gagne » suffit a les ecraser, le bloc PR135 reste donc intact comme preuve d'origine.
# Les donnees restent privees : benchmark_prep/invoices/, benchmark_prep/references/, data/invoices/
# et tous les autres repertoire results/product-review1xx/ ne sont pas touches par ce bloc.
# Crible de confidentialite des 19 chemins (results/product-review147/pr147-pr110-audit.json) :
